      "stem": "The temperature rises from $-7\\degree C$ to $5\\degree C$. What is the temperature change?",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "$2\\degree C$" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "$-12\\degree C$" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "$12\\degree C$" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "$-2\\degree C$" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "c",
      "explanation": "Temperature change $= 5 - (-7) = 5 + 7 = 12\\degree C$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "knowledge-check",
      "stem": "What is $(-2)^3$?",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "$-8$" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "$-6$" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "$6$" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "$8$" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "a",
      "explanation": "$(-2)^3 = (-2) \\times (-2) \\times (-2) = 4 \\times (-2) = -8$. An odd power of a negative number gives a negative result."
